Lab‑Grade Test Protocol

System: TSECE–Suprakernel EngineAuthor: C. Matthew BlackwellPurpose: Empirically validate stability, provenance, and feedback behavior of the substrate‑coupled architecture.

1. Objectives

Objective 1: Verify Hamiltonian stability under long‑run D‑Matter evolution.

Objective 2: Confirm encrypted state ledger correctness and non‑forgery.

Objective 3: Validate ZKP/PXI transition gating (no unverified state accepted).

Objective 4: Test AIL feedback and circuit breaker behavior under induced drift.

2. Test Environment

Hardware:

Multi‑core CPU with thermal sensors

Optional GPU for geometry workloads

Software:

TSECE engine (ingest, solver, encryption, feedback modules)

Suprakernel integration layer

Monitoring:

High‑resolution logging of:

(P(t)), (\epsilon_{\text{oxy}}), (\epsilon_{\text{field}}), (T_{\text{drift}}), (H_{\text{sub}})

(H), (\Delta H_t), constraint violations, ledger entries, ZKP results

3. Test Cases

3.1 Hamiltonian Stability Test

Setup:

Initialize manifold (q_0, p_0) with known configuration.

Run step_dmatter(q, p, dt) for (N) steps (e.g., (N = 10^5)).

Data:

Record (H_t), (\Delta H_t), constraint violations.

Pass Criteria:

(|\Delta H_t|) remains within defined stability band for majority of steps.

No unbounded growth in (H_t).

3.2 Ledger Integrity & Non‑Forgery Test

Setup:

For each step, call hash_state(X_t, A_t) and write_ledger_entry(...).

Store all (L_t) in an external audit store.

Tamper Test:

Manually alter one historical (L_t).

Attempt to replay or verify using verify_transition(...).

Pass Criteria:

Tampered entries fail verification.

Untampered entries pass consistently.

3.3 ZKP/PXI Transition Gate Test

Setup:

Generate valid proof (\pi_t) for a known transition.

Generate invalid or random (\pi'_t).

Procedure:

Call verify_transition(X_t, h_t, π_t) and verify_transition(X_t, h_t, π'_t).

Route accepted transitions into Suprakernel via report_verified_transition(...).

Pass Criteria:

Only valid proofs yield ok = true.

No transition is recorded without ok = true.

3.4 Feedback Loop & Circuit Breaker Test

Setup:

Induce controlled drift by perturbing (q, p) or artificially increasing (\Delta H_t).

Procedure:

Call evaluate_drift(dH_t) and monitor status.

When status = "critical", ensure engage_circuit_breaker(reason) is invoked.

Confirm Suprakernel receives notify_circuit_breaker(status, reason).

Pass Criteria:

Circuit breaker reliably engages at or above threshold.

Normal operation resumes only when drift returns to stable band.

4. Data Analysis

Metrics:

Drift distribution over time

Ledger verification success/failure rates

False‑accept / false‑reject rates for ZKP

Circuit breaker latency and reliability

Outcome:

Determine whether the engine behaves as a stable, substrate‑verified, cryptographically‑anchored simulation system under lab conditions.

